  "worked_solution": "To find the constant of proportionality, we first need to choose a point $(x,y)$ on the graph. Here, let's choose the point $(5,4).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14184158/assets/468695422e5c641a076c8f2889f926a7c633c69e98c96fdefb07b2c19c2acbdc.png)\n\nNow, we can find the constant of proportionality by computing the ratio of the $y$-coordinate to the $x$-coordinate, as follows:\n\n$$\nk=\\frac{y}{x}=\\frac{4}{5}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the constant of proportionality is $k=\\frac{4}{5}.$",
